    "body": "Closes #115.\n\nImplements ADR-013: px, em, rem, %, and auto horizontal margins now resolve at layout time via a context-aware parse_length. Pages with real CSS spacing render the way their authors wrote them.\n\n## The gap this fixes\n\nAfter PR #113, margin: 10px 20px renders. But anything that is not Npx silently becomes 0: padding: 2em, margin: 5em auto, width: 50%, font-size: 1.5em all collapse.\n\nTesting example.com against Firefox surfaced the gap. Its div has margin: 5em auto and padding: 2em. In Firefox it centers horizontally with breathing room. In our browser, before this PR, it hugged the top-left corner at 600px wide with zero spacing.\n\n## The fix\n\nDelivered in three stages within one commit:\n\n### Stage A - LengthContext, parse_length, is_auto\n\n- New LengthContext struct: font_size, parent_font_size, root_font_size, parent_content_width, on_font_size_property.\n- parse_length(value, ctx) resolves:\n  - px -> absolute\n  - em -> own font_size, or parent_font_size when on_font_size_property\n  - rem -> root_font_size\n  - % -> parent_content_width * n/100\n- is_auto() detects the auto keyword.\n- parse_px kept for compatibility. Removal deferred.\n- 7 new [length] test cases.\n\n### Stage B - cascade and layout font-size atomic change\n\n- cascade.cpp: font-size removed from kInheritedProperties. Cascade no longer inherits font-size as a raw string.\n- layout.cpp: layout_element threads parent_font_size and root_font_size. font_size_of() computes own font-size (em on font-size resolves against parent).\n- fill_sides uses parse_length per side with the correct context.\n- No new tests. Existing tests pass unchanged.\n\n### Stage C - auto horizontal margin centering\n\n- Auto margins center the box: available = parent_content_width - content_w - padding - border. Each auto side gets available (single) or available/2 (both).\n- box.x and content_x recomputed from final margins so children position inside the centered box.\n- 4 new [layout][auto] test cases.\n\n## Verification\n\n- ./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[layout]\" -> 27 cases, 116 assertions, all pass\n- ./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[length]\" -> 7 cases, 20 assertions, all pass\n- ./build/tests/honeybee_tests \"[layout][auto]\" -> 4 cases, 19 assertions, all pass\n- ./build/tests/honeybee_tests -> 154 cases, 644 assertions, all pass (was 143/605 before this PR)\n- grep -rl \"lexbor/\" src/ still returns exactly src/renderer/html/convert.cpp\n\n## Visual verification\n\nLoaded example.com in the built binary. Before this PR: 600px div hugging the top-left corner with zero spacing. After this PR: div centered horizontally, 32px padding inside the div, 80px space above it. Recognizably the same layout Firefox produces.\n\n## Deferred (per ADR-013)\n\n- Viewport units: vw, vh, vmin, vmax\n- Font-relative units: ch, ex\n- Absolute units: pt, cm, mm, in\n- calc(), min(), max(), clamp()\n- height: %\n- auto for width, margin-top, margin-bottom\n\n## Next\n\nWith length units landed, the next ADR candidates:\n\n1. UA stylesheet - h1 at 2em, p margin 1em 0, body margin 8px. High visible payoff; the ADR-013 em support makes this possible.\n2. Inline formatting - span, a, em, text wrapping. The biggest structural gap for real pages.\n3. Pseudo-classes (:link, :visited, :hover) - enables links to look like links.\n\nEach its own ADR + issue + PR.\n",
